    "created_at": "2019-07-15T21:35:19Z",
    "updated_at": "2019-07-15T21:35:19Z",
    "body": "> should we also have it for `<input dir>` as well?\r\n\r\nI must shamefully admit I forgot about `dir`, but that makes sense. That is no more predictable to the author than the language.\r\n\r\n> I just now realized you are proposing `lang=auto` as the opt-in, which already is the case for `dir=auto`\r\n\r\nWell, `dir=auto` uses a simple heuristic based on the content, but doesn't allow the UA to take further information into account, and gets something like “<span dir=rtl>HTML הוא מדהים</span>“ (\"HTML is awesome\" in Hebrew) wrong.\r\n\r\n> I thought you were proposing something that might be of more convenience than an HTML attribute, is that an option?\r\n\r\nWhat do you have in mind?",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
