    "created_at": "2019-07-17T14:39:31Z",
    "updated_at": "2019-07-17T14:39:31Z",
    "body": "Seeing as we currently have `[dir]`, `:dir()`, `direction` (which does not yet define `auto`) and `[lang]`, `:lang()` but we do not have `language` - so maybe that, for consistency? But that'd mean enabling authors to specify a document's language in CSS? Which might not be desirable or even web compatible for what I know.\r\n\r\nPerhaps, input-specific properties e.g. `input-lang(uage)` &plus; `input-dir(ection)` so you don't have to do (even if we had `auto` value for `direction` and a new `language` property):\r\n ```\r\ninput,\r\ntextarea,\r\n[contenteditable] {\r\n  direction: auto;\r\n  language: auto;\r\n}\r\n\r\n// or\r\n<input dir=\"auto\">\r\n```\r\n\r\nbut rather\r\n\r\n```\r\n:root {\r\n  input-direction: auto;\r\n  input-language: auto;\r\n}\r\n```",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
