    "updated_at": "2019-07-17T15:10:32Z",
    "body": "Regardless of the exact name, I don't think this belongs to CSS. This is the wrong layer, and it really belongs in HTML. Which attribute/value should activate it is debatable, but this is not style.\r\n\r\n(The direction property is already somewhat misplaced, and the spec recommends that authors do not use it. It's kept mainly to be able to layout XML dialects that do not have a dir attribute.)",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
