    "body": "@Malvoz There is already an `dirname` attribute that HTML page authors can use to cause the user agent to emit the direction the user used in a form on submit (it names the name of the attribute that will contain the dir). The `dir` attribute of an element presumably is connected to base direction from dir=auto or other interfaces that the user agent provides, so you can just style dir \"normally\"\r\n\r\nLanguage *is* a problem here. Font selection, for example, can be important when inputting text or other language sensitive operations. Heuristics are not that helpful on a form field, since the input tends to be short (it starts out with 0 characters to evaluate). Peeking at the input method/keyboard and speller (which the user agent can do) would be significantly helpful (I've written exactly that code into several UI frameworks--the keyboard is usually a better hint than the page language, although note that I'm typing this using my Japanese IME).",
